MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Frankie Valli & The 4 Seasons feels like a natural next choice because I want familiar mid-sixties songs, much like AM Gold: The Mid-'60s.",
    "Hall & Oates and Rock And Roll Never Forgets fit the melodic pop and familiar rock mood reflected in my Cars and classic-rock listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Shania Twain's hits do not fit my current interest in older pop and rock, while Enya and relaxing classical music suggest a different listening mood.",
    "Tornado, Based on a True Story..., and collections without a recognizable artist leave me unsure whether I would know or enjoy the songs; that uncertainty keeps me from choosing them now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat greatest-hits collections as appealing to me regardless of whose songs they contain.",
    "My varied listening history seems to have been taken as a reason to offer several different listening moods, although I am looking for familiar pop and rock today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection between my mid-sixties collection, Simon & Garfunkel, and nostalgic hits matters more to me than simply finding another compilation.",
    "Recognizing the artist and expecting familiar songs strongly affects whether I choose something; a hits label alone does not give me that confidence."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly understood my interest in nostalgic hits but stretched it beyond the familiar pop and rock I want right now."
}
